    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Set once (green)\n1. In **Settings**, set `source`: `email`, `app` or `typed`.\n2. Email: open **Read new mail**, pick your mail account and turn the node on. In **Settings**, set `sender` to the site's mail address, and `subjectHas`.\n3. App: upload `docs/samples/authenticator-code.steps.json` on your import form and approve it. Pick **RPA Desktop Runner** on **Read the code from the app**.\n4. Typed: nothing to set. While the bot waits, open the **Type a code** form and type the code.\n5. In **⋯ → Settings**, set **Save successful production executions** to **Do not save**. Publish this workflow.\n6. On the bot's RPA node, choose this workflow in **Options → One-Time Code Workflow**.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "3d6f1a20-7b4c-4e8a-9c11-000000000618",
      "name": "Set once",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -620
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works (grey)\nThe RPA node starts this workflow when the site asks for a code, with `requestedAt` and `account` (the user name). It must return one item with `code`, within **Code Timeout** on the RPA node (120 seconds). `giveUpSeconds` ends the search before that. Each source looks again every 5 seconds. A Wait node would pause the bot's run, so there is none. With successful executions not saved (step 5), codes do not stay in them.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "3d6f1a20-7b4c-4e8a-9c11-000000000619",
      "name": "How it works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        520,
        -620
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Per account (grey)\nFor the app, `appEntry` is the entry to copy in the authenticator app. It is the account's user name until you change it: make it an expression such as `({ 'user-a': 'Entry A' })[$json.account] ?? $json.account`. `source` may differ per account the same way.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "3d6f1a20-7b4c-4e8a-9c11-00000000061a",
      "name": "Per account",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        220
      ]
    }
